commit 44efa6828cbbf48135df2eb8a078c22bab2a7e20
Author: Nguyễn Anh Kiệt <84920219+koniz-dev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Sat Sep 26 16:04:47 2026 +0700

    refactor(auth)!: require tokenStore on AuthLocalDataSourceImpl (#244)
    
    BREAKING CHANGE: `AuthLocalDataSourceImpl` no longer accepts
    `SecureStorageService? secureStorageService`; `ITokenStore tokenStore` is
    required. Adopters who passed the secure-storage form wrap it:
    `tokenStore: SecureTokenStore(secureStorageService)`. Behaviour is
    identical - the constructor built exactly that object. See CHANGELOG.md.
    
    The fallback was the last concrete storage type this file named, it taught
    two ways to build the same object, and it deferred a missing-argument error
    from the analyzer to a runtime `ArgumentError`. It was also the sole reason
    koniz-dev/flutter-starter#179's criterion 1, written as the literal
    `grep -rn "StorageService" lib/features`, still matched a
    `*_local_datasource.dart`.
    
    No production call site used it: `auth_providers.dart` has always passed
    `tokenStore:`. Three test call sites did and now wrap the service. No test
    existed for the `ArgumentError`, so none was deleted.
    
    Refs koniz-dev/flutter-starter#196
    Refs koniz-dev/flutter-starter#179
    
    Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

